Integration done. Three notes on what happened:

**Judgment: JA** — this session carried a lot of durable knowledge (root causes with mechanisms, two live bugs that predated the work, a corrected self-diagnosis, and a project state change).

**Note on concurrency:** a parallel integration of the 2026-08-27 session was writing into the same files while I worked. It created `entity/moriosolutions-website.md` as a dangling link target, which I had independently chosen as the name — our content merged cleanly, and I left its additions untouched.

**One contradiction I could not resolve, only flag:** that parallel page measured that ports 3000–3002 *do* time out from outside, i.e. ufw is not bypassed. My session measured that 3001 *was* reachable from inside the nginx container while 3010 was not, under the same ufw rule. I recorded the observation as fact and the iptables explanation (INPUT vs. FORWARD/DOCKER chain) as an unverified hypothesis with `#prüfen`, rather than picking a winner. Same for the `scp .env.production → .env` line, which the 08-20 page says was removed and this session found present.

